# Accepted risks for the seeds image ONLY (ghcr.io/kinnexus-au/simulator-seeds,
# base bedasoftware/fhirsnake@sha256:cc98b6ba... — upstream's newest build,
# pushed 2026-07-29). Applied via the `trivyignores` input in seeds.yaml and
# trivy-scheduled.yaml; never merge these entries into the shared .trivyignore:
# the same packages are reachable in other scan targets.
#
# Justification (execution profile, not absence of the flaw): the image runs
# solely as the `interpolate-init-bundle` init container
# (infra/kustomize/aidbox.yaml). It executes `fhirsnake export` over the seed
# YAML baked into the image plus environment variables, writes
# /data/initBundle.json, and exits before Aidbox starts. No listening socket
# (server mode is never invoked), no untrusted input. Its only network I/O is
# outbound to the first-party in-cluster questionnaire-converter service
# (digest-pinned, deployed from these same manifests) to convert the seed
# Questionnaires — no untrusted peers.
#
# All flagged packages are fhirsnake's own dependencies with fixes released;
# fixing them requires an upstream dependency refresh and image rebuild.
#
# Remove entries when upstream publishes a rebuilt fhirsnake image and the
# FROM pin in resources/Dockerfile is bumped: re-run the gate scan and delete
# whatever no longer fires. Re-triage the whole file if the image's command or
# usage changes (an external converter URL, watch/server mode, anything beyond
# the init container).

